WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:08.503
If neurons are made in excess and the target decides who stays, what exactly would

2
00:00:08.503 --> 00:00:09.503
the target be doing?

3
00:00:10.383 --> 00:00:13.403
The neurotrophic hypothesis puts it in one line.

4
00:00:14.363 --> 00:00:18.503
Neurons compete for a limiting amount of neurotrophic factor for survival.

5
00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:21.177
The targets supply it.

6
00:00:21.957 --> 00:00:23.937
Axons that reach these tissues take it up.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:29.777
Neurons that get too little die by apoptosis, a built-in program of cell death.

8
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.150
Stated this way, the hypothesis makes predictions you can check one at a time.

9
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.493
Remove the target, and more neurons die.

10
00:00:39.453 --> 00:00:42.193
Hamburger's wing-bud removal, read across time, fits.

11
00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.927
Add target, and fewer die.

12
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:47.617
Add factor, and fewer die.

13
00:00:48.557 --> 00:00:49.917
Remove factor, and more die.

14
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:55.647
And most of the death should happen around the time axons reach the target and begin

15
00:00:55.647 --> 00:00:56.647
to compete.

16
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.310
That is a checklist.

17
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:02.690
The rest of this lesson tests the first four items, one at a time.

18
00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:08.793
In 1976, Margaret Hollyday and Viktor Hamburger tested the second item.

19
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:14.083
They grafted an extra leg onto chick embryos, beside the normal one.

20
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:20.737
Predict. With more target, what should happen to the lumbar motor neurons, before

21
00:01:20.737 --> 00:01:22.377
the normal loss and after it?

22
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:32.767
At day 6, before the normal loss, there were no more motor neurons than usual.

23
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:38.630
Later, more motor neurons remained, in embryos whose grafts moved vigorously.

24
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:44.653
They proposed a word for it.

25
00:01:44.653 --> 00:01:48.053
Hypo-thanasia: not extra birth, but reduced death.

26
00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:54.833
One caution. That result came from motor neurons, and they do not depend on NGF.

27
00:01:55.917 --> 00:01:58.477
So the graft supports a limiting target resource.

28
00:01:59.377 --> 00:02:01.077
It says nothing about which molecule.

29
00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:07.247
Hollyday and Hamburger left open whether the scarce resource was synaptic space or a

30
00:02:07.247 --> 00:02:08.247
trophic agent.

31
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:10.817
Hold on to the shape of the idea.

32
00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:14.437
Make too many, then let the target keep what it can feed.

33
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.150
The next tests need a molecule.

34
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.570
That molecule is nerve growth factor, NGF.

35
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.700
Takeaway: the hypothesis predicts reduced death, not extra birth.

36
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.040
When counts change, tests must ask which happened.
